<title>FRANCE: U.N. clears sale of 100,000 T French wheat to Iraq.</title>
<headline>U.N. clears sale of 100,000 T French wheat to Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. cleared this week the sale of 100,000 tonnes of French soft wheat to Iraq under a scheme allowing Baghdad to sell oil in exchange for food and medicine, a French official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The U.N. approved one or two days ago the export of 100,000 tonnes of soft wheat,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>France had submitted applications for the sale of 300,000 tonnes of French wheat under the U.N oil for food deal. The wheat, sold in December, was due for shipment in January and February.</p>
<p>The official said the U.N clearance would allow shipment to start this month.  </p>
<p>Exporters were still awaiting a reply on the fate of the remaining 200,000 tonnes of wheat sold under the December contract.</p>
<p>Including the December sale, France has sold close to 600,000 tonnes of French wheat to Iraq. Additional contracts are for shipment in March and April.</p>
<p>But exporters have not yet asked the government to forward applications for U.N approval of these additional sales.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
